.TH STOMARCHY 1 "May 2026" "stomarchy 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stomarchy \- manage Omarchy config tweaks without replacing the defaults
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stomarchy
.RI COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stomarchy
stores user changes as diff-only runtime tweaks under
.IR ~/.config/stomarchy
and imports those tweaks from config files restored from Omarchy defaults.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add [--dry-run] FILE
Generate a tweak from FILE by comparing it with the matching Omarchy original.
Without
.BR --dry-run ,
the target file is restored from the Omarchy original and a Stomarchy tweak
import block is appended.
.TP
.B link [FILE]
Link checked-out tweaks into local target files without recalculating them.
.TP
.B remove FILE
Delete the matching tweak and restore FILE from the Omarchy original.
.TP
.B sync [--dry-run]
Copy current Omarchy originals into local target files and reattach tweak import
blocks.
With
.BR --dry-run ,
print the changes that would be made without writing files.
.TP
.B wipe
Restore every local target with a current Omarchy original back to the baseline
Omarchy file, without appending tweak imports. Tracked tweaks are left intact.
.TP
.B status
Show tweak health, including linked, unlinked, stale, no-op, unsupported, and
missing-original states.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/stomarchy
Directory containing tracked tweaks.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/omarchy/config
Default Omarchy config mirror used as the comparison and restore source.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the user's config directory. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B STOMARCHY_OMARCHY_CONFIG_DIR
Overrides the Omarchy original config directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview a tweak:
.B stomarchy add --dry-run ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf
.TP
Track and wire a tweak:
.B stomarchy add ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf
.TP
Preview an Omarchy sync:
.B stomarchy sync --dry-run
.TP
Return local targets to Omarchy baselines:
.B stomarchy wipe
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR diff (1)
